{
  "_note": "Reference signals for text-layer labels. SONARA, MAEST and promoted Rhythm Lab classifiers are proxies, not ground truth: a poor score can mean the label is weak or that the proxy does not describe it. Direction 1 means the label should rank the reference high, -1 means low.",
  "_independence": "What a reference can prove. 'orthogonal' means it measures a different kind of signal than the label name, so agreement is evidence. 'echo' means the reference is a head carrying the label's own genre name, learned from the same web tag conventions as the text towers: their errors correlate, so agreement shows a shared vocabulary rather than a working label, and the verdict is capped at 'consistent'.",
  "_blind": "Text families that must not be scored against this reference. A promoted classifier trained on CLAP audio features is not independent of a CLAP text label, so scoring them together measures self-agreement. Listed families are skipped for that label in both the cross-check and the fusion benchmark.",
  "harmony/dissonant": {
    "kind": "numeric",
    "source": "sonara",
    "field": "dissonance_score",
    "direction": 1,
    "independence": "orthogonal"
  },
  "harmony/drone": {
    "kind": "numeric",
